  "behavior_proved": [
    "the public Windows Manager startup service owns one bounded MTA worker with one active request and one FIFO successor",
    "pre-dispatch cancellation, active caller cancellation, hard deadlines, successor promotion, and concurrent shutdown drain have deterministic native tests",
    "terminal cancellation owns the COM call until it drains, pulses CoCancelCall on the owning apartment, and fails stopped after the documented five-second ownership bound",
    "the exact current-user registration uses one deterministic task path and the same path as its Source-qualified ownership URI, including safe purpose suffixes",
    "native BSTR, VARIANT, interface, process-command-line, duration, HRESULT, account-name, and current-SID boundaries are bounded and RAII-owned",
    "foreign Source or URI returns an ownership-only ForeignConflict before enabled, state, history, principal, trigger, action, or settings projection",
    "absent trigger repetition and zero expiration serialize without invalid Task Scheduler XML, while the unified scheduling engine and account-name normalization round-trip to the canonical model",
    "the current-machine lifecycle passed Missing to Ready to Disabled, injected owned priority drift, observed Drifted, repaired through ReplaceOwned and TASK_UPDATE while preserving Disabled, enabled, started the fixture, verified its exact sentinel, removed the task, and returned to Missing",
    "ownership and postcondition races for repair, enablement, start, and remove fail closed in the handler tests",
    "the lifecycle cleanup reopens only the deterministic registration, verifies exact path plus Source and URI, refuses foreign ownership, and left zero scheduled tasks and zero temporary homes",
    "the related process-command-line boundary tests and the Windows infrastructure public-header self-containment target also pass"
  ],
